A||||26||Gokart||Can you make your own shortened shifter?||||||
Z||000000||Gokart||05-28-99||06:45 PM||||I am close to making a purchase for a shortened shifter kit, but was wondering what stops me from disconnecting my own and hack sawing it to the length I want, reconnecting the knob and putting it back? Any suggestions or tips? TIA
Z||000001||Bruce||05-28-99||06:53 PM||||Check through this forum- one of the members manufactures the shifters, plus the knob, for $25. Certainly saves you a lot of hassle for peanuts!!
Z||000002||Bruce||05-28-99||06:59 PM||||Specifically:<p>Tom McElroy<br>12249 Hart St.<br>No. Hollywood, Ca. 91605<p>He includes the shift knob free, if i didn't mention. He seems like a pretty good sort.<br>bb
Z||000003||theogre||05-28-99||07:36 PM||||if you want a shorted stick. there is nothing stopping you from chopping it.<p>if you want a shorter throw, then the stick must be replaced. The short throw stick has a diferant pivot point.
Z||000004||Yellow85||05-29-99||04:33 AM||||If you want to have a straight stick, cut weld part and take stick out from mount. Then cut bent part of stick and just weld to the mount. you might also need to cut bottom of shift knob and shift boot, if you make it really sort(but don't make it too short, you will have little trouble every time you shift in to reverse, i didn't like it so i change to little longer one).  If you want stick like factory's(i mean same position as factory)just chop it make it shorter then put some tape around it(top part)and put knob back.  That's it!! either way cost me $0. If you have a time try it, it is very easy to do and it's free. Also, short shift is a lot easier for me to shift.
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||05-29-99||09:35 PM||||Well I was bored and decided to do it. I grabbed the dremal and started cutting. Took a while but got a nice cut. I started a small fire from the sparks but no biggie. The wife came running in and started giving me the third degree :0) I cut the weld and then cut the stick right above the turn. Tomorrow I will weld it together and install my "short" shifter. Who said it doesnt cost anything???? It cost me about 10 cents for the 3 cutoff wheels...LOL
Z||000006||Gokart||05-30-99||05:14 AM||||Bruce, I got a hold of Tom and decided to try his. It's on its way and I will let you all know how it turned out. 
Z||000007||Bruce||05-30-99||11:46 AM||||Did you check if this is short throw, as well? That's what I assumed, so we'll see.<br>I should get mine by Tues., so we'll compare notes.
Z||000008||Gokart||05-30-99||07:08 PM||||Will do
Z||000009||Bruce||06-02-99||07:54 PM||||Installed mine today- working around the back-up light mechanism was tough, but I made it. I like the feel and response the shifter makes; so, next project: the exhaust system.<br>Let me know how your installation went.
Z||000010||fierosound||11-30-1999||07:19 PM||||I decided to make my own shortened shifter.  I went to the wreckers to get on "to work on" rather than the one in the car.  I checked out 2 Fiero wrecks (84s) and started taking one off.  It turned out this was already shortened by about 1 1/2"!!  All I had to do, was install it in my car!!  Quick, easy... cost only $15  (aboy US$11.75) ||||reg||10
Z||000011||fiero56||11-30-1999||09:41 PM||||I seem to remember hearing somehere that the stick in '84 Fieros was shorter than the following model years.  Anyone else hear this or have one?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||11-30-1999||10:29 PM||||I bought a short shifter from Tom and then did a little extra work on it to make the travel even less. Where the shift cable attached to the shifter, I cut the shifter and extended this part down about 13 mm. This made for even shorter travel than just the shortened handle alone. If anyone is interested, I will post pictures to show how the modification is done. You will need access to a welder for this. I also took one of my old Civic shift knobs and drilled it out to fit the Fiero shaft. It looks and feels much better than the hard plastic original one.||||reg||3
Z||000013||WKDFIRO||12-01-1999||12:34 AM||||Ive had a short shifter for years and also put the Camaro leather shifter knob on it. LOOK GREAT AND STOCK! Problem is that you can't really go back when you have a short shifter. I was a co-driver for a friend's Fiero on a long trip with and he had the stock height. I never got used to it in all of those 600 miles that I drove, I couldn't quick shift like I could on mine! It just feels perfect.||||reg||6
Z||000014||Monkeyman||12-01-1999||03:00 AM||||I have an auto, but I got a leather shifter knob out of a late model Camaro.  Wow, it's neat!  And it only cost me $10 (that's $3,495.63 to you Canadian guys).||||reg||1
Z||000015||Mark||12-01-1999||07:45 PM||||Cooter, I'm interested in how you extended the cable attachment point to reduce the throw.  Please post the pictures! Also, is the shifting effort noticably affected by these mods?  I would prefer to shorten my shifter about 1.5" from the top, but I can't find the metric die to rethread the shaft.  Has anyone else crossed this bridge? ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cooter||12-01-1999||08:09 PM||||I will get some pic's soon- give me a few days because I will pull the shifter out of the car to give a better view of the modification- I dont think you guys with the backup light switch on the shifter will be able to do this modification. You will see what I mean when you see the pic's.||||reg||1
Z||000017||RZURCTN||12-01-1999||08:16 PM||||By the way fellas', 84 Fieros already have the shorter shifter as someone suspected.  I shortened the one in my 84 and can't wait to find out how it'll work.   Additionally, Fierodave has shortened shifters too.  You can e-mail him if you need anything.  Check out his post in the Mall.  Just my $0.02  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by RZURCTN (edited 12-02-1999).]||||reg||3
Z||000018||TOM||12-01-1999||09:14 PM||||You mean fierodave has them. That doesnt mean he makes them.||||reg||1
Z||000019||RZURCTN||12-02-1999||06:22 PM||||Sorry Tom!  I wasn't aware of Daves source at the time!  I stand corrected!  Thanks.||||reg||12
Z||000020||BigBoyToys||12-02-1999||06:48 PM||||Monkeyman: If you like the leather Camaro auto shifter knob try the Trans Am auto T-Handle. I made the swap on my IROC and what a great fit to rest your hand. I got mine out of an auto salvage yard for pennies. Just my 2 cents.||||reg||10
Z||000021||Mark||12-02-1999||07:57 PM||||Cooter,<P>I thought you already had photos.  I certainly didn't expect you to dismantle your car!  I'd settle for a little more verbal discription of the shifter mod!||||reg||1
Z||000022||batboy||12-02-1999||08:51 PM||||Mark, let Cooter dismantle his car, it may keep his brother from borrowing it (ha ha).<P>Monkey and BigBoy, the auto shifter knob in the Batmobile has seen better days. Tell me more about swapping the Camaro or Trans Am knob. What year(s) of donor car and did it require any modification?||||reg||1
Z||000023||BigBoyToys||12-02-1999||10:33 PM||||Batboy my IROC is an 88 third generation and the doaner TA was also third gen. Basically just a direct fit. To remove I place the stick in first so that I can view the front of the knob, about an inch up from the base is a square wire u shaped clip that just pulls out (I used needlenose pliers) it shaped like a large staple. Then the knob just lifts off. No modification was needed but when installing the T-Handle alignment was with release button pointing towards 10 o'clock rather than parrallel to the dash. Hope that helps alittle. Just go slow, clean mating surfaces and maybe a slight smear of lithium grease or vasoline.   ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Monkeyman||12-03-1999||12:38 AM||||BigBoyToys--My car had the original T-handle on it (non-leather, of course).  Didn't like the "T".  That's the main reason I went looking for a different handle.  Also, I'm building a custom dash and I wanted more clearance.  Good idea, though.<P>Batboy--You can also use a flat screwdriver to remove the "staple".  Just be VERY careful.  And definitely use some lithium grease when you install it if you ever intend to remove it again.  I tried 3 different cars before I found one I could actually get off!  Seems like the leather ones are a tighter fit.  My wifes' is the same except for the leather and hers was almost loose.||||reg||1
Z||000025||WKDFIRO||12-03-1999||04:02 AM||||Mark,<P>Just cut the section you don't want and use the threaded end don't throw it away just use it!||||reg||4
Z||000026||batboy||12-03-1999||04:01 PM||||Thanks for the info guys. I've had the auto shifter and middle console off two different Fieros before, so I know about the U clip, but maybe others don't know how to remove them. Next time I'm in the auto boneyard, I'll check the Trans Ams and Camaros out.||||reg||1
